    <!-- http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#population_cardinality_unit -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#population_cardinality_unit">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#Cardinality_unit"/>
        <iso21972:symbol>pc</iso21972:symbol>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">population_cardinality_unit is depicted to be an instance of Cardinality_unit, which is the unit of measure for the cardinality of a set defined by a Population (defined in the next clause), and is associated with the symbol “pc”. For example, 1100pc represents a population cardinality (or size) of 1100. This document takes advantage of prefix notations to scale the numbers by defining units of measures: kilopc, megapc and gigapc, which are multiples of population_cardinality_unit. 1.1 kilopc represents 1100 pc.</dc:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#population_ratio_unit -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#population_ratio_unit">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#Unit_division"/>
        <iso21972:denominator rdf:resource="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#population_cardinality_unit"/>
        <iso21972:numerator rdf:resource="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/ISO21972/iso21972#population_cardinality_unit"/>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">population_ratio_unit is defined to be an instance of Unit_division. It has two properties:
• whose range is restricted to being a population_cardinality_unit;
• whose range is restricted to being a population_cardinality_unit.

In other words, a population ratio is the ratio of two population cardinalities (i.e., number of members/elements in each population)</dc:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


